# mcp__codebase_memory_trace_path — codebase-memory/trace_path

Trace callers/callees, data flow, or cross-service paths. Defaults exclude tests and resolver evidence. Rows keep qn/hop with explicit totals, relations, and continuations.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  function_name: string;
  project: string;
  direction?: "inbound" | "outbound" | "both";
  depth?: number;
  /** Rows/page; gte flags the 5000-node engine ceiling. */
  limit?: number;
  /** Sizing hint; hard ceiling is 4 UTF-8 bytes/token. Evidence/args yield before nearest graph rows. */
  max_output_tokens?: number;
  /** Pass next/next_cursor with traversal args unchanged; budget may increase. */
  cursor?: string;
  /** calls; argument-aware data_flow; service edges; topology: infra objects, routes, controllers (from a Resource/Route); deploy: what CI jobs and scripts run and deploy; run: what a Service runs (image, Dockerfile, program, env). */
  mode?: "calls" | "data_flow" | "cross_service" | "topology" | "deploy" | "run";
  /** data_flow parameter filter. */
  parameter_name?: string;
  edge_types?: string[];
  /** Add hop-risk labels. */
  risk_labels?: boolean;
  include_tests?: boolean;
  /** tree chooses smaller complete direct/grouped output; json uses stable grouped tables. */
  format?: "tree" | "json";
  /** Add resolver class and confidence. */
  include_evidence?: boolean;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__codebase_memory_trace_path.

