# mcp__codebase_memory_query_graph — codebase-memory/query_graph

Read-only Cypher for multi-hop, aggregation, complexity, or cross-service analysis. Default: 200 visible rows with exact/lower-bound totals and truncation; continue safely with next_cursor. graph=missed is a file tree of flagged coverage gaps; absence is not proof of completeness. Use get_graph_schema(diagnostics=full) for properties.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** Cypher query */
  query: string;
  project: string;
  /** code graph (default) or missed coverage-gap file tree. */
  graph?: "code" | "missed";
  /** Visible rows (default 200; max 99998); 0 uses the legacy maximum. Evaluation is unchanged. */
  max_rows?: number;
  /** Live compatibility paging; cannot be combined with cursor. */
  offset?: number;
  /** Snapshot continuation; keep query/project/graph. Format, budget, and max_rows may change. */
  cursor?: string;
  /** Sizing hint; hard ceiling is 4 UTF-8 bytes/token. Rows stay whole. */
  max_output_tokens?: number;
  /** tree may use local @N+suffix prefix refs; json uses direct strings. */
  format?: "tree" | "json";
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__codebase_memory_query_graph.

